   "evidence": "runs() validates `row.get(\"head_branch\") != branch` only. The repository id is fetched in reconcile() but never compared against run rows. test_wrong_branch_or_status_filter_is_rejected covers only a differently named branch.",
   "file": "tauceti_worker/workflow_backstop.py",
   "fix": "Reject (or skip) rows whose `head_repository.id` differs from the repository's `id`, and preferably accept only runs whose `event` is `schedule`, `workflow_dispatch` or `push`. Add a test with a same-named fork-branch row.",
   "issue": "`GitHub.runs` checks only `row['head_branch'] == branch`. A fork pull_request run from a fork branch named `main` matches GitHub's name-only `branch` filter, so it can be taken as the latest run (decision `recent`) or, if stuck queued/waiting, as the active run (decision `active`). Either way the default-branch maintenance dispatch is suppressed, contrary to the README's 'on the repository's current default branch' scope.",
   "line": 94
  }
